    "motion": {
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 3300,
      "w": 440,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Motion (not drawn): rows, panels and pills use a 0.2 shear with upright text and a 10 px radius. Most moves ease OutQuint over 300–500 ms; small pops use OutElastic. The selected list panel slides 25 px left in 400 ms; the header slides in from the left in 600 ms. Leaderboard rows reorder with a 450 ms slide; your row widens 20 px with a pop. The pace flash holds 3 s, then fades back to your time. Missing avatars fade to the real image in 300 ms."
    },
    "data": {
      "x": 2200,
      "y": 3300,
      "w": 440,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "teal",
      "text": "Sample data: titles and creators come from our port list. Every other number, player name, avatar and music title is invented. All art is a placeholder (five scenes stand in for each game's real background) except the delicious fruit, which is the real sprite. Times are tick counts at 50 per second, shown to hundredths."
    },
    "open": {
      "x": 2720,
      "y": 3300,
      "w": 440,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "orange",
      "text": "Still open: the status set (Ranked / Unranked / …), the mod list (SD, MR, HB, NB, FL, SS, SL, FA are examples of the kinds in docs/product.md, not decisions), the star rating formula, whether the death heatmap stays, the overall rank on the player card (needs the performance system) and the result badges (ideas, no system yet)."
    }
  },
